<article class="env-lemma" id="0C0P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C0P">Lemma <span data-tag="0C0P">58.30.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a flat proper morphism with geometrically connected fibres. Let $s' \leadsto s$ be a specialization. If $X_ s$ is geometrically reduced, then the specialization map $sp : \pi _1(X_{\overline{s}'}) \to \pi _1(X_{\overline{s}})$ is surjective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $X_ s$ is geometrically reduced, we may assume all fibres are geometrically reduced after possibly shrinking $S$, see More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C0E" data-tag="0C0E">37.26.7</a>. Let $\mathcal{O}_{S, s} \to A \to \kappa (\overline{s}')$ be as in the construction of the specialization map, see Section <a href="/tag/0BUP" data-tag="0BUP">58.16</a>. Thus it suffices to show that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \pi _1(X_{\overline{s}'}) \to \pi _1(X_ A)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is surjective. This follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/0C0J" data-tag="0C0J">58.15.2</a> and $\pi _1(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)) = \{ 1\} $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>